  "body": "Operation picking is now a mode (#1514). A viewport click changes the open operation's geometry only while its Geometry tab shows or a pick row (a boundary entry) is armed. On every other tab the selection is locked: the click changes nothing, does not fall through to a model select that would swap the dialog, hover lights nothing, a Ctrl/Shift pick box is not armed, and the dialog says \"Picking off - selection locked\" (or \"Picking on - clicks edit the selection\"). Selection changes stay undoable `SetOperationGeometry` commands; the lock is derived from `op_tab` and the drafts, never stored. Setup-page picks (locate, points, plane, axis, WCS) are their own modes and are not locked.\n\nFiles: `crates/ui/src/interact.rs` (`op_pick_locked`, guard in `pick_at`, hover), `box_pick.rs`, `egui_app/geo_page.rs` + `op_page.rs` (indicator), `egui_app/tests/pick_mode.rs`, `docs/decisions/1514-pick-mode.md`. Reuses the #1520 area without touching `geo_hover`.\n\nPinning tests (`egui_app::tests::pick_mode`): locked click on Heights leaves picks, dialog and queue untouched (also in Model mode); same click on the Geometry tab replaces the pick and Undo restores it; armed boundary row unlocks off-tab; the indicator text on/off (structural).\n\nMutation checks: guard in `pick_at` disabled -> locked-click test fails; `op_pick_locked` always false -> 3 tests fail (locked click, boundary, indicator); boundary exemption dropped -> boundary test fails; indicator inverted -> indicator test fails.\n\nNot exercised: the real GUI (headless only); the box-drag lock only by code path (`box_pick::armed`), not a drag test. Fork synced at current upstream main (fd2f4f30).\n\nChangelog: Operation picking is a mode: viewport clicks edit an operation's geometry only on its Geometry tab (or with a pick row armed); other tabs lock the selection and say \"Picking off\" (#1514, PR #1528)\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1514\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
